{"id": "EUVD-2026-82237", "enisaUuid": "6f7248a0-8a05-32ed-ad81-78e562c44626", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nplatform/x86: dell-wmi-base: Fix handling of ultra performance key\n\nThe commit message of commit 5fbd827eb9c2 (\"platform/x86: dell-wmi: Recognise or support new switches\")\nstates that the ultra performance key contains additional data\nafter the type and code fields. The event data passed to\ndell_wmi_process_key() is already parsed, so \"buffer\" already\nstarts after those two fields.\n\nUse the correct index for accessing the first data field to avoid\na potential buffer overread.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:11:32", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:52:00", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/30674a7bbf20311a0c4edd5edb9526ef1eecc692", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ace1a687ea9ea70d17e3089ca173acfa1ec24412", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/16a82add1918d3aae1e0b68c0a983b6fc64f5062", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/392c19faec6bf4cb72fb02322e2a61e198dd8f72", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/adfd6846bea13667ff28f8aaf00c32fbd69825ab"], "aliases": ["GHSA-3wx5-9x5h-8qmh", "CVE-2026-93129"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "22bb59c5-8c5e-3ec5-a367-f4527f73ce25", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.16"}, {"id": "24591576-1214-32a9-80cb-eb4b31962f2c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "2e4574bd-51d9-34b7-8a86-317496595058", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "352220f7-7e7b-385c-aa45-a8b3c329c87f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "4dc7d16a-58dc-3702-b251-0eed1c92a835", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5fbd827eb9c224c33a5f263ee543a75fe957faa3 <16a82